meta {
  name: 07 - Respond (unauthenticated - 401)
  type: http
  seq: 7
}
post {
  url: {{base_url}}/respond
  body: json
  auth: none
}
body:json {
  {
    "patient_id": "{{patient_with_documents}}",
    "question": "do you recommend surgery?"
  }
}
docs {
  No Authorization header on purpose. Expect 401 before any work runs.

  This closes the Week 1 finding. The grader flagged missing TESTS on the
  authorization boundary; the actual defect was that /ask and /chat had no auth
  check at all, and /respond inherited it. All three now reject unauthenticated
  requests, and the denial is audited with a denial_reason.
}
